       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** That is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose within the 2,550 mg/day limit.** Give me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it.\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me the corrected dose. I can add a note about titration or monitoring to the order if you'd like."
